			"notes": "Minecraft **26.3** (Fabric) port with DisplayHUD 2.2 changes.\n\n### Requirements\n- Java 25, Fabric Loader 0.20.1+, Fabric API 0.164.0+26.3, Polymer 0.18.4+26.3\n- Clients: vanilla 26.3 (resource pack via Polymer)\n\n### Changes\n- Ported to 26.3 (unobfuscated, no mappings), Loom 1.18.2, Gradle 9.7.1\n- DisplayHUD 2.2: packet-only virtual displays merged into passenger packets, `GlobalHud`, `setAboveHand`, `updateWhenDataChanged`, `removeWhenPlayerDied`, `setGlowing`, text opacity/background; auto resend on respawn/dimension change\n- 26.3 core/post shaders from DisplayHUD v26_3, merged with ShaderFX text shader\n- ShaderFX updated to the 26.1 shaderfx implementation\n- Dynamic FOV shader is now opt-in (`dynamicFovShader: true` in `config/minigame-lib/shaderfx.json`)\n- Client visual gametest (`runClientGameTest`)\n\n### Breaking\n- `DisplayHudManager` defaults: unit 1→100, screen 1920x1080, alignment gap 10000→1000000\n- `OwnerOnlyEntityAttachment` removed; `runSmokeServer` harness removed\n\n### Verification\n- `test` + `runGameTest`: all 7 required tests pass; shaders validated offline with glslc\n- In-game visual check not yet completed"
		},
